WEBVTT

00:07:29.653 --> 00:07:33.240
Or if hip hop gave voice
to the environment or future generations

00:07:33.282 --> 00:07:35.451
who can't speak for themselves.

00:07:36.118 --> 00:07:39.330
Now using popular music
to raise awareness about climate change

00:07:39.371 --> 00:07:41.123
has already started happening.

00:07:41.123 --> 00:07:43.209
Two years ago,
the New York Times reported

00:07:43.250 --> 00:07:46.837
that there have been at least
192 references to climate change

00:07:46.879 --> 00:07:50.049
in any song that has been
made by any artist

00:07:50.090 --> 00:07:52.885
who has been featured on any
of Billboard's domestic charts

00:07:52.885 --> 00:07:54.678
over the past two decades.

00:07:54.678 --> 00:07:55.846
So not a lot.

00:07:56.180 --> 00:07:58.307
And I only knew a handful of the songs.

00:07:58.307 --> 00:08:00.392
We need a lot more of that.